 K2.5 - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-moonshot-ai-kimi-k2-5.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": 1769472000, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 4, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 383755}, "snippet": "", "title": "Kimi K2.5 - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/en_en/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-moonshot-ai-kimi-k2-5.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 5, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 383755}, "snippet": "", "title": "Chat Completions API - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-chat-completions.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 6, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 383755}, "snippet": "", "title": "Amazon Bedrock endpoints and quotas - AWS General Reference", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/bedrock.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 7, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 383755}, "snippet": "", "title": "APIs supported by Amazon Bedrock - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/us_en/bedrock/latest/userguide/apis.html"}], "type": "search_result_group"}], "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=docs.aws.amazon.com&sz=128"], "turn_exchange_id": "2fcd9245-c365-427e-9faf-a918260d95f2", "working_turn_id": "2fcd9245-c365-427e-9faf-a918260d95f2"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web.run"}, "name": "web.run", "role": "tool"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": [""]}, "create_time": 1790214435.5898, "end_turn": null, "id": "d4ead47a-f234-42b3-b002-16c10f9e4176", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "7b94a161-2c0f-4256-abd5-afb6262ca4d7", "reasoning_start_time": 1790214429.2365365, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "reasoning_title": "Searching the web", "reasoning_titles": ["Searching the web"], "request_id": "af66b728-8fe7-482b-90f2-460c75e81a8c", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_model_queries": {"queries": ["site:docs.aws.amazon.com bedrock mantle regions endpoint us-east-2 CreateInference API key 2026", "site:docs.aws.amazon.com Amazon Bedrock model access region availability Kimi K2.5 GLM 5 DeepSeek V3.2 us-east-2", "site:docs.aws.amazon.com bedrock api keys bearer token bedrock mantle OpenAI compatible endpoint"], "type": "search_model_queries"}, "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["globe"], "turn_exchange_id": "2fcd9245-c365-427e-9faf-a918260d95f2", "working_turn_id": "2fcd9245-c365-427e-9faf-a918260d95f2"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. Based on what you’ve described, I would **not** treat the $140+ credit as the problem yet. Credits determine whether usage is billable; they do not explain a basic connectivity/authentication failure.\n\nThe most likely fault domain is exactly where you’re pointing: **region + endpoint + model invocation path**, especially because Bedrock now has two distinct OpenAI-compatible surfaces.\n\n### The clean diagnostic model\n\nFor something like **Kimi K2.5 in Ohio**, AWS currently documents all three of these as valid:\n\n- Region: `us-east-2`\n- Model ID: `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n- Mantle base URL: `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1` citeturn383755search1turn383755search3\n\nKimi K2.5 is explicitly available **in-region in `us-east-2`**, so we do **not** need to invent a cross-region deployment/profile just to call it there. citeturn383755search0\n\nThat gives us a known-good target.\n\nThe confusing part is that AWS now has:\n\n**Classic/runtime OpenAI path**\n`https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/openai/v1`\n\nand\n\n**Mantle path**\n`https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`\n\nThose are **not interchangeable**. They use different authorization actions and potentially different quotas/access state. AWS documents `bedrock:InvokeModel` for the runtime endpoint versus `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference` for Mantle. citeturn383755search1turn383755search5\n\nSo if we changed credentials while also changing endpoints, SDK config, regions, or model IDs, we can very easily get ourselves into a situation where **every individual component is legitimate but the combination is wrong**.\n\n## I would reduce this to one golden-path test\n\nForget OpenCode, GLM configuration, agents, deployments, and the GCE stack for the moment.\n\nTest exactly:\n\n```text\nREGION\nus-east-2\n\nENDPOINT\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n\nMODEL\nmoonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n\nAPI\n/chat/completions\n\nAUTH\ncurrent Amazon Bedrock API key\n```\n\nAWS explicitly says the OpenAI SDK configuration for this path is:\n\n```text\nOPENAI_API_KEY=<Amazon Bedrock API key>\nOPENAI_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\nciteturn383755search1\n\nThen one microscopic request:\n\n```text\nSay exactly: BEDROCK_OK\n```\n\nIf that fails, **the exact error tells us which layer is broken**:\n\n| Result | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| DNS / connection failure | endpoint/network |\n| 401 | credential/API-key problem |\n| 403 | IAM / bearer-token permission / model authorization |\n| 404 | wrong URL/API route/model identifier |\n| validation error | request payload/API mismatch |\n| model unavailable | regional/model-access issue |\n| 429 | quota/throttling |\n| `BEDROCK_OK` | AWS path works; GCE/OpenCode integration is the problem |\n\nThere is one credential wrinkle worth flagging. Current AWS documentation distinguishes the permission to **use an API key against Mantle** as `bedrock-mantle:CallWithBearerToken`, while actual inference authorization is associated with the Mantle inference permissions. So generating a fresh-looking credential does **not automatically prove that the principal can use it against that endpoint**. citeturn383755search2\n\nAnd I think this explains why this has felt absurdly complicated: we may have been debugging **four variables simultaneously**:\n\n**credential → endpoint → region → model/API**\n\ninstead of freezing three and testing one.\n\n### What I want us to do now\n\nKeep Luce doing the full Truth Tower.\n\nFor our working lane, I would freeze **`us-east-2 + Mantle + Kimi K2.5` as the control case**. If that single call works, we immediately know the $140 runway is usable and can work outward from there into GLM/DeepSeek/OpenCode. If it doesn't work, give me the **exact sanitized error response** from that one call—not the whole history—and we can usually classify it in one pass.\n\nAWS itself confirms that `us-east-2` supports the Mantle endpoint, and Kimi K2.5, DeepSeek V3.2, and several other models are actually available there. So your instinct that this is probably a **configuration/region/invocation-path issue rather than “Bedrock simply doesn't work”** is technically plausible. citeturn383755search0turn383755search1 memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790214436.108765, "end_turn": true, "id": "593abb11-3217-4884-a042-6473c7429e5c", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "xvbsdp", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "ic2t5g", "preview_language": null, "pre