Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-amazon-nova-lite.html"}], "type": "search_result_group"}], "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=aws.amazon.com&sz=128", "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=docs.aws.amazon.com&sz=128"], "turn_exchange_id": "a6516564-ea32-4267-9569-fcbc7919fa1c", "working_turn_id": "a6516564-ea32-4267-9569-fcbc7919fa1c"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web.run"}, "name": "web.run", "role": "tool"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": [""]}, "create_time": 1790216077.8336112, "end_turn": null, "id": "9debb40e-ca00-42e3-90a7-3cbf3519161c", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "2732bf6d-1774-43ce-86af-0751e2cf3dad", "reasoning_start_time": 1790216076.4932375, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "reasoning_title": "Searching Amazon Bedrock pricing model prices Kimi K2.5 DeepSeek V3.2 GLM 5 Nova 2 Lite September 2026", "reasoning_titles": ["Searching Amazon Bedrock pricing model prices Kimi K2.5 DeepSeek V3.2 GLM 5 Nova 2 Lite September 2026"], "request_id": "d820f2d2-59f3-49b1-a446-dfc8bab4b757", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_model_queries": {"queries": ["Amazon Bedrock pricing model prices Kimi K2.5 DeepSeek V3.2 GLM 5 Nova 2 Lite September 2026", "site:docs.aws.amazon.com bedrock list foundation models pricing Kimi K2.5 GLM 5 DeepSeek V3.2 Nova 2 Lite"], "type": "search_model_queries"}, "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["globe"], "turn_exchange_id": "a6516564-ea32-4267-9569-fcbc7919fa1c", "working_turn_id": "a6516564-ea32-4267-9569-fcbc7919fa1c"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. **This is exactly the right time for a super-extraction.** We have working access now, so instead of guessing from docs, we can extract **your actual live model inventory**, then reconcile it against AWS pricing and sort it by cost.\n\nAnd the Nova error you just hit is **PowerShell/AWS CLI JSON quoting**, not Bedrock. The JSON arrived at AWS with the quotation marks stripped:\n\n```text\n[{role:user,content:[{text:Return exactly: NOVA_OK}]}]\n```\n\nSo for the Nova test, I want to stop fighting inline JSON entirely.\n\n## 1. Fix the Nova test cleanly\n\nRun this:\n\n```powershell\n@'\n{\n  \"modelId\": \"amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Return exactly: NOVA_OK\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"inferenceConfig\": {\n    \"maxTokens\": 20,\n    \"temperature\": 0\n  }\n}\n'@ | Set-Content \"$env:TEMP\\nova-test.json\" -Encoding ascii\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock-runtime converse `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --cli-input-json \"file://$env:TEMP/nova-test.json\"\n```\n\nThat removes PowerShell quoting from the equation completely.\n\nIf it returns `NOVA_OK`, we have the Amazon-native runtime lane proven end-to-end too.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Now do the **full Bedrock extraction**\n\nI want **two inventories**, because we have now empirically established that AWS exposes different families through different surfaces.\n\n### Mantle inventory\n\nRun:\n\n```powershell\n$MantleModels = (Invoke-RestMethod `\n  -Method Get `\n  -Uri \"$env:OPENAI_BASE_URL/models\" `\n  -Headers @{ Authorization = \"Bearer $env:OPENAI_API_KEY\" }\n).data\n\n$MantleModels |\nSort-Object id |\nSelect-Object id,status,owned_by,created |\nFormat-Table -AutoSize\n```\n\nThen save it:\n\n```powershell\n$MantleModels |\nSort-Object id |\nSelect-Object id,status,owned_by,created |\nExport-Csv \"$env:USERPROFILE\\Desktop\\bedrock_mantle_us-east-2.csv\" -NoTypeInformation\n```\n\n### Classic Bedrock/runtime inventory\n\nRun:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock list-foundation-models `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --output json |\nOut-File \"$env:USERPROFILE\\Desktop\\bedrock_runtime_us-east-2.json\" -Encoding utf8\n```\n\nAnd a readable table:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock list-foundation-models `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --query \"modelSummaries[].{Provider:providerName,Model:modelName,ModelId:modelId,Status:modelLifecycle.status}\" `\n  --output table\n```\n\nThat gives us the **actual account-visible estate** rather than AWS's theoretical catalog.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Cost landscape — the interesting part\n\nFor `us-east-2`, AWS's current Standard-tier pricing already gives us some very interesting options. citeturn258904search0\n\n| Model | Input / 1M | Output / 1M | Relative role |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| **Nemotron Nano 2** | **$0.06** | **$0.23** | ultra-cheap utility |\n| **Nemotron 3 Nano 30B** | **$0.06** | **$0.24** | cheap utility/reasoning |\n| **GLM 4.7 Flash** | **$0.07** | **$0.40** | ridiculously cheap worker |\n| **Nemotron 3 Super 120B** | **$0.15** | **$0.65** | inexpensive stronger worker |\n| **DeepSeek V3.2** | **$0.62** | **$1.85** | strong reasoning/coding |\n| **GLM 4.7** | **$0.60** | **$2.20** | general reasoning |\n| **Kimi K2 Thinking** | **$0.60** | **$2.50** | deliberate reasoning |\n| **Kimi K2.5** | **$0.60** | **$3.00** | strong general/coding |\n| **GLM 5** | **$1.00** | **$3.20** | heavier reasoning |\n| **Kimi K3 Global CRIS** | **$3.00** | **$15.00** | premium heavy model |\n| **Kimi K3 US CRIS** | **$3.30** | **$16.50** | premium US-routed K3 |\n\nKimi K3 also gets much cheaper on cache reads — AWS currently lists **$0.30/M cached tokens globally** — so K3 could make economic sense for highly repetitive long-context workloads even though its raw headline price is much higher. citeturn258904search6\n\nDeepSeek V3.2 is particularly interesting for us: **164K context**, up to **8K output**, Mantle and runtime support, at $0.62/$1.85 in the US regions. citeturn258904search1\n\nAnd Nova 2 Lite is a different beast: AWS documents a **1M-token context window and 64K max output**, plus prompt caching on the runtime endpoint. citeturn258904search2turn258904search3\n\n## Which means…\n\nWith **$159.26 of AWS credits**, we are not just limping along.\n\nAt current Standard pricing, purely as rough token-budget intuition:\n\n- GLM 4.7 Flash could consume **enormous** volume before exhausting that balance.\n- Kimi 2.5 is still cheap enough for sustained serious use.\n- DeepSeek V3.2 is cheaper on output than Kimi 2.5.\n- K3 should probably be treated as a **premium escalation lane**, not the default hammer.\n- Nova 2 Lite may be extremely useful for **very-large-context extraction/reconciliation** if its invocation lane proves healthy.\n\nAnd AWS supports **Flex at 50% below Standard** for several of these model families, while Priority is 75% above Standard, so there's another cost-control lever once we know which workloads tolerate Flex latency. citeturn258904search0\n\n### What I want from Don\n\nFirst run the **Nova file-based test**.\n\nThen run both inventory extractions.\n\nIf you give me the Mantle CSV and runtime JSON—or simply paste the inventories—I can turn this into the real artifact we need:\n\n**Amazon Bedrock GCE Model Estate — us-east-2**\n\nwith:\n\n**model → provider → exact model ID → endpoint → context → max output → cost → cache cost → service tiers → live-tested status → recommended workload class**\n\nsorted from **cheapest to most expensive**.\n\nThat will finally turn the $159.26 from “some AWS credit somewhere” into an actual **GCE runtime budget and routing map**. memcite"]}, "creat