"default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "41261ea8-8e45-429a-9ae8-46d0a6a54dfa", "reasoning_start_time": 1790216412.8008432, "reasoning_status": "is_reasoning", "reasoning_title": "Searching AWS Bedrock cross-region inference IAM permissions InvokeModel inference profile foundation model Operation not allowed ValidationException Nova 2 Lite", "reasoning_titles": ["Searching AWS Bedrock cross-region inference IAM permissions InvokeModel inference profile foundation model Operation not allowed ValidationException Nova 2 Lite", "Searching AWS Bedrock Nova 2 Lite Converse Operation not allowed inference profile us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0"], "request_id": "21df0eec-9973-449c-b2d7-d045f4b5f6cc", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_model_queries": {"queries": ["AWS Bedrock cross-region inference IAM permissions InvokeModel inference profile foundation model Operation not allowed ValidationException Nova 2 Lite", "AWS Bedrock Nova 2 Lite Converse Operation not allowed inference profile us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0"], "type": "search_model_queries"}, "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["globe"], "turn_exchange_id": "4085d781-ca6c-4553-9bcd-c37ab6411e5d", "working_turn_id": "4085d781-ca6c-4553-9bcd-c37ab6411e5d"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Exactly. **That result kills the “wrong region/profile doesn’t exist” hypothesis.**\n\nYour account in `us-east-2` can resolve an **ACTIVE US cross-region inference profile** for Nova 2 Lite, and AWS is explicitly telling us the profile can route to:\n\n- `us-east-1`\n- `us-east-2`\n- `us-west-2`\n\nSo the remaining suspect is now **authorization across the inference profile and all destination-region foundation-model ARNs**, not basic region discovery. AWS requires `bedrock:InvokeModel` permission on the inference profile **and** on the foundation model in the source and every destination region in the profile. A deny/SCP on even one destination can break cross-region inference. citeturn108679search0turn108679search1\n\nThis is very Azure-like conceptually: **one logical deployment/profile, multiple regional backends**, except AWS makes the IAM evaluation across those routing targets more explicit.\n\n## Next step: inspect Don’s actual Bedrock permissions\n\nRun this:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-attached-user-policies `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --output table\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\naws iam list-user-policies `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --output table\n```\n\nDo **not** change IAM yet. I just want to see whether `PeteW` has something broad like:\n\n```text\nAmazonBedrockFullAccess\n```\n\nor whether we're dealing with custom inline policies.\n\nIf `AmazonBedrockFullAccess` is already attached, then we pivot immediately to **SCP / explicit deny / model access**.\n\nIf it is **not** attached, the likely defect is that the current policy allows Mantle but does not grant the classic Bedrock runtime action:\n\n```text\nbedrock:InvokeModel\n```\n\nacross:\n\n```text\narn:aws:bedrock:us-east-2:280768229421:inference-profile/us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\narn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\narn:aws:bedrock:us-east-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\narn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2::foundation-model/amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\nAWS documents that exact permission pattern for geographic cross-region inference. citeturn108679search0turn108679search6\n\nSo our troubleshooting tree is now beautifully narrow:\n\n**Mantle/Kimi works ✅**  \n**Nova profile exists ✅**  \n**Nova profile ACTIVE ✅**  \n**Profile routes across three US regions ✅**  \n**Converse still blocked ❌**  \n→ **IAM/SCP authorization is now the primary suspect.**\n\nRun those two IAM listing commands. That should tell us very quickly which branch we're on."]}, "create_time": 1790216418.658573, "end_turn": true, "id": "f8a38237-188f-4c20-9fd2-a5acdd8ed1ca", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "70di9i", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "ews88i", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "kd569h", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "v89x0g", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "30c7to", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 723, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 1, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Supported Regions and models for inference profiles - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-profiles-support.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "Geographic cross-Region inference - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn108679search0turn108679search1", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": ["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-cross-region-inference.html", "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/geographic-c