_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "Qwen3 Coder Next - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-qwen-qwen3-coder-next.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": 1786492800, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 1, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "Daybreak Blue: GPT-5.6 Sol - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/en_en/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-daybreak-blue-56-sol.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": 1783900800, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 2, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "GPT-5.6 Sol - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/un_es/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-56-sol.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": 1786492800, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 3, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "Daybreak Blue: GPT-5.6 Sol - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/hi_in/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-daybreak-blue-56-sol.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 4, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "Regional availability by models - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 5, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "Web Search - Amazon Bedrock", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/web-search.html"}, {"attribution": "docs.aws.amazon.com", "pub_date": null, "ref_id": {"ref_index": 6, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 336747}, "snippet": "", "title": "Amazon Bedrock endpoints and quotas - AWS General Reference", "type": "search_result", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/bedrock.html"}], "type": "search_result_group"}], "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=docs.aws.amazon.com&sz=128"], "turn_exchange_id": "6a7bbd05-97a6-43cb-9c1c-6165aeba9e84", "working_turn_id": "6a7bbd05-97a6-43cb-9c1c-6165aeba9e84"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yep — that quota dump is the smoking gun, and it is worth preserving exactly as **account-level evidence**:\n\n> `QuotaAppliedAtLevel: ACCOUNT` + `Value: 0.0` + several critical Nova request/token quotas marked `Adjustable: false`.\n\nThat is much stronger than “maybe Nova is having a region issue.” The account can discover Nova, resolve the inference profile, and authenticate — but the classic Bedrock Runtime lane is effectively shut for those Nova inference dimensions.\n\nSo: **leave Nova alone for now.** We have a healthy Mantle estate and $159.26 of runway.\n\n## Bedrock Mantle estate — first-pass cost map\n\nI’m separating **verified-live**, **visible**, and **runtime-blocked** so we don’t accidentally promote inventory visibility into proven execution.\n\n| Model | Mantle state | Standard input / 1M | Standard output / 1M | Context | Best GCE use |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| **GLM 4.7 Flash** | Visible | ~$0.07 | ~$0.40 | 203K | cheap utility / extraction |\n| **Nemotron Super 3 120B** | Visible | ~$0.15 | ~$0.65 | 256K | cheap agentic worker |\n| **GPT-5.6 Luna** | Visible | **$0.22** | **$1.32** | up to 1M family context | fast general worker |\n| **DeepSeek V3.2** | Visible | ~$0.62 | ~$1.85 | 164K | reasoning / coding |\n| **GLM 4.7** | Visible | ~$0.60 | ~$2.20 | 203K | general reasoning |\n| **Kimi K2 Thinking** | Visible | ~$0.60 | ~$2.50 | long-context | deliberate reasoning |\n| **Grok 4.3** | Visible | **$1.25** | **$2.50** | **1M** | agentic reasoning / huge context |\n| **Kimi K2.5** | **LIVE TEST PASSED** | ~$0.60 | ~$3.00 | **256K** | coding + reasoning default |\n| **GLM 5** | Visible | ~$1.00 | ~$3.20 | **200K** | systems / architecture |\n| **GPT-5.6 Sol** | Visible | **$4.40** | **$22.00** | **1M** | premium escalation only |\n\nThe AWS docs independently confirm the capability side: Kimi K2.5 is 256K context/16K output; DeepSeek V3.2 is 164K/8K; GLM 5 is 200K; Grok 4.3 is 1M and configurable-reasoning; GPT-5.6 Sol is 1M context. citeturn760214search6turn760214search2turn421442search3turn760214search5turn336747search2\n\nAWS also confirms **GPT-5.6 Luna** is radically cheaper than Sol: $0.22/M input and $1.32/M output for short-context in-region traffic, versus Sol at $4.40/M input and $22/M output. citeturn421442search7turn336747search2\n\n## The immediate GCE economics are excellent\n\nTake a representative **100K-input / 10K-output** job:\n\n- GLM 4.7 Flash: about **$0.011**\n- Nemotron Super: about **$0.0215**\n- GPT-5.6 Luna: about **$0.035**\n- DeepSeek V3.2: about **$0.0805**\n- Kimi K2.5: about **$0.090**\n- GLM 5: about **$0.132**\n- Grok 4.3: about **$0.150**\n- GPT-5.6 Sol: about **$0.66**\n\nThat means your **$159.26** is not emergency scraps. At Kimi K2.5-type usage, it represents a lot of serious work. At GLM Flash/Luna utility workloads, it represents a *huge* amount.\n\n### The architecture that falls out of this\n\nI would not make one Bedrock model do everything.\n\nThe natural economic lanes are:\n\n- **Cheap utility:** `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n- **Cheap strong worker:** `nvidia.nemotron-super-3-120b`\n- **Fast OpenAI worker:** `openai.gpt-5.6-luna`\n- **Reasoning/coding value:** `deepseek.v3.2`\n- **Primary Kimi lane:** `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n- **Deliberate Kimi reasoning:** `moonshotai.kimi-k2-thinking`\n- **Architecture/heavy systems:** `zai.glm-5`\n- **Huge-context alternative:** `xai.grok-4.3`\n- **Premium exception:** `openai.gpt-5.6-sol`\n\nThat is **capability routing**, not changing seat authority. MODEL ≠ SEAT. memcite\n\n## There is one major endpoint trap we need to document\n\nNot every Mantle model uses the same path.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nKimi / GLM / DeepSeek\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\nBut AWS documents **Grok 4.3** on:\n\n```text\nhttps://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/openai/v1\n```\n\nand GPT-5.6 Sol also uses the `/openai/v1` family. citeturn760214search5turn336747search2\n\nThat is exactly the kind of thing that can recreate today’s mess if we build one universal provider configuration and assume every model speaks through the identical base path.\n\n## Next move: make this extraction empirical\n\nBefore we wire anything into GCE, I’d run a **micro-probe matrix** against the 8 models we actually care about.\n\nSame prompt:\n\n```text\nReturn exactly: BEDROCK_OK\n```\n\nSame tiny output.\n\nCapture:\n\n```text\nmodel_id\nendpoint/base-path\nsuccess/failure\nlatency\nprompt_tokens\ncompletion_tokens\nservice_tier\n```\n\nNo more than a few dozen tokens each.\n\nThen our estate changes from:\n\n**AVAILABLE**\n\nto:\n\n**LIVE VERIFIED**\n\nmodel by model.\n\nAfter that, I can build you the final **Bedrock GCE Runtime Matrix** sorted three ways:\n\n**cost → capability → preferred GCE workload**, including exact model IDs, endpoint variants, context limits, cache economics, and fallback order.\n\nAnd the Nova evidence gets quarantined as:\n\n**CLASSIC RUNTIME / ACCOUNT QUOTA GATED — DO NOT TROUBLESHOOT FURTHER UNTIL AWS CHANGES ACCOUNT QUOTAS.**"]}, "create_time": 1790216779.500851, "end_turn": true, "id": "8b1c89ae-c666-4b2c-a87d-a5f290aac768", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "9cxytv", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id