"channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yeah — **from a user experience standpoint, it’s pretty rough** because AWS is letting you see the model, resolve the profile, and authenticate successfully, while the actual token-generating quotas sit at **0**. The resulting error — `ValidationException: Operation not allowed` — does a terrible job of telling you the real reason.\n\nAnd no, **switching regions is very unlikely to be the fix** for this Nova problem. Your own profile already proves Nova 2 Lite can route across `us-east-1`, `us-east-2`, and `us-west-2`; the blocker is the **account-level Bedrock Runtime quota**, not simple regional availability.\n\nWhat AWS says now is:\n\n- adjustable Bedrock Runtime quotas can be requested through **Service Quotas**;\n- some on-demand/model-invocation quotas are **not adjustable directly** in Service Quotas, but AWS explicitly says you can still submit a **limit increase request** for consideration;\n- AWS may set defaults based on things like **regional factors, payment history, fraud/abuse controls, and prior quota approvals**. citeturn179100search0turn179100search3\n\nSo your intuition is basically right: **you’ll need to request quota/provisioning for the Runtime/Nova lane** rather than keep rotating keys or trying regions.\n\nOn the “free tier credit” part, I’d phrase it carefully: the credits themselves are not what blocks Bedrock Runtime. AWS says Free Tier credits can apply toward eligible paid usage, and after credits are exhausted, normal billing applies if the account is on the paid plan. But AWS can still assign very low or zero service quotas independently of whether a payment method exists. citeturn179100search9\n\nIn other words:\n\n> **Payment method + credits ≠ guaranteed nonzero Bedrock Runtime quota.**\n\nFor the Nova quotas that show `Adjustable: true`, we can request an increase directly. For the ones showing `Adjustable: false`, AWS’s Nova documentation says you can still use the **limit increase form / Support path** to be considered. citeturn179100search0\n\nSo when you’re ready, I’d treat this as a separate cleanup item:\n\n**“Enable Bedrock Runtime/Nova quotas for account 280768229421”**\n\nwith the evidence package we already have: active profile, admin IAM, no permissions boundary, successful Mantle inference, and account-level Nova quotas at zero. That should make the support request much cleaner than starting from “Nova says operation not allowed.”"]}, "create_time": 1790216855.478965, "end_turn": true, "id": "61e1e33c-bc08-4364-a1b3-bdb7ccdc89e4", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/quotas.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 1081, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 3, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Quotas for the bedrock-runtime endpoint - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/en_en/bedrock/latest/userguide/quotas-runtime.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "Quotas for Amazon Nova - Amazon Nova", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/quotas.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "matched_text": "citeturn179100search0turn179100search3", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": ["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/en_en/bedrock/latest/userguide/quotas-runtime.html", "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/en_en/bedrock/latest/userguide/quotas-runtime.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com", "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/quotas.html", "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/quotas.ht