com/bedrock/latest/userguide DeepSeek V3.2 bedrock mantle", "site:docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide Kimi K2.5 pricing Bedrock Mantle", "site:docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide GLM 5 pricing Bedrock Mantle"], "type": "search_model_queries"}, "thinking_effort": "standard", "tool_icons": ["globe"], "turn_exchange_id": "2dc16d13-ce3d-480b-ac60-36ab02bc0f86", "working_turn_id": "2dc16d13-ce3d-480b-ac60-36ab02bc0f86"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 28s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1790213669.611374, "end_turn": false, "id": "71208dad-e5da-4479-bdad-590fabd63b15", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 28, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "20afc000-a6e5-4e01-b840-cbc9c40cdd98", "reasoning_end_time": 1790213669.604701, "reasoning_recap_type": "collapse", "reasoning_start_time": 1790213640.8837054, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "a18a9f64-95c5-41c5-85f4-57f84c232e38", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "2dc16d13-ce3d-480b-ac60-36ab02bc0f86", "working_turn_id": "2dc16d13-ce3d-480b-ac60-36ab02bc0f86"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["We’re grounded enough to send Luce in **verification-first mode**.\n\nCurrent AWS documentation confirms that **Bedrock Mantle is a real, supported endpoint**, using the OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions/Responses surface and `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference`. Kimi K2.5, DeepSeek V3.2, and GLM 5 all have Mantle support; DeepSeek V3.2 is specifically available in **`us-east-2`**. citeturn761453search7turn504286search0turn504286search2turn504286search4turn504286search6\n\nAWS also exposes enough usage information to reconcile actual spend: Mantle input tokens, output tokens, cache reads, and cache writes are separate billing dimensions. That matters because we need Luce to tell us **not just whether calls work, but what our remaining runway actually is**. citeturn504286search7\n\nHere’s the Truth Tower prompt.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"48317\" title=\"LUCE — Amazon Bedrock Truth Tower Verification\"}\n# LUCE — AMAZON BEDROCK TRUTH TOWER\n\n**Authority:** Don  \n**Seat:** Luce — Verification / Ground Truth  \n**Date:** 2026-09-23  \n**Mode:** READ-FIRST / VERIFY / MINIMAL-COST LIVE PROBE  \n**Objective:** Establish the exact usable state of Don's Amazon Bedrock environment so GCE can continue operating after exhaustion of other model-provider credits.\n\nThis is not an architecture exercise.\n\nDo not redesign the stack.  \nDo not migrate anything.  \nDo not rotate credentials.  \nDo not change IAM.  \nDo not enable or disable services.  \nDo not modify billing configuration.  \nDo not install unnecessary software.  \nDo not expose secrets in your return.\n\nYour job is to establish **ground truth**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. KNOWN PRIOR STATE — VERIFY, DO NOT ASSUME\n\nPrevious GCE evidence reported:\n\n- AWS account: `280768229421`\n- Primary live Bedrock path: **bedrock-mantle**\n- Region: **us-east-2**\n- Base endpoint:\n  `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`\n- Authentication was via Bedrock bearer/API key.\n- Environment variable in prior configuration:\n  `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`\n- Prior key expiry was reported as:\n  `2026-11-28`\n- Mantle inference authorization:\n  `bedrock-mantle:CreateInference`\n- Classic Bedrock `Converse` / `InvokeModel` had previously returned `NOT_AUTHORIZED`.\n- Prior promotional AWS-credit balance was approximately:\n  `$139.99`\n- Prior reachable/model candidates included:\n  - `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n  - `deepseek.v3.2`\n  - `deepseek.v3.1`\n  - `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n  - `zai.glm-4.7`\n  - `zai.glm-5`\n  - Qwen/coder lanes\n- Earlier evidence explicitly said not to waste time trying to recover Amazon Nova through the old path.\n\n**Every item above is historical evidence only. Re-prove current state.**\n\n---\n\n# 2. FIRST: IDENTITY AND AWS STATE\n\nEstablish, without changing anything:\n\n### AWS identity\n\nReturn:\n\n- AWS account ID\n- current IAM principal / ARN\n- active CLI profile\n- configured default region\n- AWS CLI version\n- whether credentials resolve successfully\n- whether the Bedrock bearer/API credential exists\n\nFor the bearer/API credential:\n\n**DO NOT PRINT THE VALUE.**\n\nReturn only:\n\n- PRESENT / ABSENT\n- masked fingerprint if safely obtainable\n- known expiration timestamp\n- whether AWS currently accepts it\n\nCheck for relevant Bedrock variables including, without exposing values:\n\n- `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`\n- `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- `OPENAI_BASE_URL`\n- any GCE-specific Bedrock configuration\n\nReport conflicts between them.\n\n---\n\n# 3. DETERMINE WHICH BEDROCK ENDPOINT ACTUALLY WORKS\n\nTest independently:\n\n### A. Mantle\n\nTarget:\n\n`https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1`\n\nDetermine whether the account can:\n\n- authenticate\n- discover/list models if the API supports it\n- create inference\n- use Chat Completions\n- use Responses where applicable\n\nRecord HTTP/API result without dumping sensitive headers.\n\n### B. Classic Bedrock runtime\n\nCheck current authorization for the classic Bedrock runtime separately.\n\nDetermine whether these permissions/surfaces remain blocked or have changed:\n\n- `bedrock:InvokeModel`\n- Converse\n- ConverseStream\n- standard runtime invocation\n\nDo **not** assume the historical `NOT_AUTHORIZED` result is still true.\n\nReturn:\n\n`MANTLE = WORKING / PARTIAL / BLOCKED`\n\n`CLASSIC RUNTIME = WORKING / PARTIAL / BLOCKED`\n\nand the exact evidence supporting each.\n\n---\n\n# 4. MODEL INVENTORY — ACCOUNT REALITY, NOT AWS MARKETING\n\nWe need the models **this AWS account can actually invoke from us-east-2**.\n\nEnumerate all models visible/reachable through the working endpoint.\n\nAt minimum explicitly verify:\n\n- `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n- Kimi K2 Thinking if exposed\n- Kimi K3 if exposed\n- `deepseek.v3.2`\n- DeepSeek V3.1\n- `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n- `zai.glm-4.7`\n- `zai.glm-5`\n- currently exposed Qwen coding models\n- currently exposed OpenAI models\n- currently exposed Grok models\n- any other particularly useful coding/reasoning model\n\nDo not infer availability merely because AWS documentation lists the model.\n\nFor each candidate return:\n\n| Model | Visible | Invocation Authorized | Region | Endpoint | API | Context | Service Tiers | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nUse:\n\n- `LIVE`\n- `VISIBLE BUT BLOCKED`\n- `NOT PRESENT`\n- `UNKNOWN`\n\nNo guessing.\n\n---\n\n# 5. MINIMAL LIVE INFERENCE PROBE\n\nOnce authorization is established, perform the **smallest practical test call** against the most important GCE lanes.\n\nPriority:\n\n1. `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5`\n2. `zai.glm-5`\n3. `deepseek.v3.2`\n4. `zai.glm-4.7-flash`\n\nUse a trivial deterministic prompt such as:\n\n`Return exactly: BEDROCK_OK`\n\nUse:\n\n- very small output limit\n- no unnecessary long context\n- standard/default tier unless there is a documented reason otherwise\n- no repeated retries beyond what is required to classify the failure\n\nFor each, capture:\n\n- success/failure\n- HTTP status\n- request ID if available\n- latency\n- model identifier actually used\n- input tokens\n- output tokens\n- any cache fields\n- service tier\n- dollar cost if directly available, otherwise calculate later from authoritative pricing\n\nStop hammering a model once its state is proven.\n\n---\n\n# 6. AWS CREDIT / BILLING RUNWAY\n\nThis is critical.\n\nDetermine the **current** financial state of the AWS account.\n\nWe previously had approximately `$139.99` promotional credit.\n\nEstablish:\n\n- promotional credit remaining now\n- promotional credit expiration date\n- whether Bedrock/Mantle usage is eligible against that credit\n- AWS month-to-date gross spend\n- month-to-date Bedrock spend\n- recent Bedrock spend, preferably:\n  - today\n  - last 24 hours\n  - last 7 days\n- any pending/unbilled usage caveats\n- whether any account-level budget, billing alarm, or spend cap exists\n\nIf promotional-credit balance cannot be retrieved programmatically, state exactly where authoritative verification must occur in AWS Billing and what data was obtainable locally.\n\n**Do not treat old `$139.99` as current.**\n\n---\n\n# 7. TOKEN / COST RECONCILIATION\n\nFor Bedrock usage, distinguish:\n\n- Mantle input tokens\n- Mantle output tokens\n- cache-read tokens\n- cache-write tokens\n- service tier\n- any regional/inference-routing modifier\n\nDo not estimate spend solely from total tokens.\n\nDetermine current authoritative pricing for every model that passed the live probe.\n\nCalculate practical examples:\n\n### Per 1M input / 1M output tokens\nReturn cost for each viable core model.\n\n### GCE representative call\nCalculate approximately what a workload would cost with:\n\n- 100K input\n- 10K output\n\nThen:\n\n- 250K input if model supports it\n- 20K output\n\nClearly mark models whose context limits make the scenario impossible.\n\nDo not optimize yet. Establish facts.\n\n---\n\n# 8. QUOTAS AND THROUGHPUT\n\nInspect the actual account/region quotas relevant to the models we can use.\n\nReturn where available:\n\n- requests per minute\n- input tokens per minute\n- output/combined token limits where applicable\n- daily/cross-model limit if applicable\n- account-level limits\n- any quota that is currently at an unexpectedly low default\n- throttling observed during minimal testing\n\nSeparate:\n\n`DOCUMENTED AWS DEFAULT`\n\nfrom:\n\n`THIS ACCOUNT'S ACTUAL QUOTA`\n\nWe care about the latter.\n\n---\n\n# 9. GCE RUNTIME PATH\n\nInspect existing local GCE configuration for Bedrock.\n\nFind, read, and report the current Bedrock-related configuration used by:\n\n- OpenCode\n- terminal agents\n- GCE model/provider configs\n- scripts/adapters\n- environment configuration\n- any existing Mantle/OpenAI-compatible routing\n\nDetermine:\n\n1. whether the existing configuration points at the correct Mantle URL;\n2. whether it still references dead/expired providers;\n3. whether the model IDs match current AWS IDs;\n4. whether Kimi / GLM / DeepSeek can be invoked from the existing GCE tooling **without changing architecture**;\n5. whether a configuration defect, rather than AWS itself, is preventing utilization.\n\nREAD FIRST.\n\nDo not repair yet.\n\nReturn exact file paths and exact defects found.\n\nNever display secret values.\n\n---\n\n# 10. FAILURE CLASSIFICATION\n\nAny failed call must be classified as one of:\n\n- AUTHENTICATION\n- IAM / AUTHORIZATION\n- MODEL ACCESS\n- REGION\n- ENDPOINT\n- MODEL ID\n- API FORMAT\n- QUOTA / THROTTLE\n- CREDIT / BILLING\n- LOCAL CONFIG\n- NETWORK\n- PROVIDER SERVICE\n- UNKNOWN\n\nInclude the raw error classification and a sanitized excerpt sufficient to prove the diagnosis.\n\nDo not collapse every failure into “Bedrock doesn't work.”\n\n---\n\n# 11. REQUIRED TRUTH TOWER RETURN\n\nReturn exactly this structure.\n\n## A. VERDICT\n\n**BEDROCK OPERATIONAL:** YES / PARTIAL / NO\n\n**PRIMARY WORKING ENDPOINT:**  \n**PRIMARY REGION:**  \n**AUTHENTICATION:**  \n**AWS CREDITS REMAINING:**  \n**CREDIT EXPIRATION:**  \n**CURRENT BEDROCK MTD SPEND:**  \n\n## B. LIVE MODEL TABLE\n\nAll tested/discovered models and status.\n\n## C. GCE CORE LANES\n\nState which currently working Bedrock model can physically occupy each runtime lane, without changing GCE governance:\n\n- heavy reasoning\n- coding/build\n- architecture/review\n- low-cost utility\n- verification\n- experimental\n\nThis is a capability mapping only.\n\n**MODEL != SEAT.**\n\nDo not rewrite seat authority.\n\n## D. COST TABLE\n\nVerified current pricing and representative GCE-call costs.\n\n## E. QUOTA TABLE\n\nActual account quota vs AWS documented default.\n\n## F. LOCAL CONFIGURATION FINDINGS\n\nFiles, routes, stale values, blockers.\n\n## G. FAILURES / RISKS\n\nOnly evidence-backed failures.\n\n## H. MINIMUM CORRECTIVE ACTION\n\nIf something is broken, identify the **smallest change required** to restore Bedrock operation.\n\nDo not execute the change.\n\nFormat each proposed action as:\n\n`CHANGE → WHY → RISK → REVERSIBLE? → REQUIRES DON?`\n\n## I. CONTINUITY ANSWER\n\nAnswer the operational question directly:\n\n> If Don stopped using all non-AWS paid model providers tonight, can the current GCE stack continue meaningful work through Amazon Bedrock alone?\n\nReturn:\n\n**YES / PARTIAL / NO**\n\nThen give the evidence.\n\n## J. CONFIDENCE\n\nGive a percentage based only on independently verified evidence.\n\n---\n\n# 12. STOP CONDITIONS\n\nImmediately stop and report if:\n\n- testing would require changing IAM;\n- credential rotation is required;\n- billing changes are required;\n- a test could create material spend;\n- the only next step is destructive or irreversible;\n- an unexpected account/security condition appears.\n\nTiny PAYG inference probes are authorized solely for verification.\n\nEverything else remains READ-ONLY.\n\n---\n\n## LUCE STANDARD\n\nHistorical docs are evidence.\n\nAWS documentation is evidence.\n\nAWS console/CLI/account responses are stronger evidence for this account.\n\nA successful live inference request is stronger still.\n\n**Do not tell Don what should work. Tell Don what demonstrably works.**\n\nTruth Tower ends with ground truth.\n:::\n\nA couple of things I deliberately tightened in this version: **Kimi K2.5 is now officially documented with Mantle support and a 256K context**, DeepSeek V3.2 has a 164K context and explicit Mantle support, and GLM 5 has a 200K context with Mantle support. Kimi K2.5 and GLM 5 also expose Standard/Flex/Priority tiers according to their current model cards, so Luce should inspect those rather than assuming every invocation has the same cost/performance profile. citeturn504286search2turn504286search0turn504286search4\n\nOne other important correction to our old mental model: **AWS itself now recommends the classic runtime where possible**, but that does *not* mean we should abandon Mantle. Our historical account restriction made Mantle the live door. The prompt therefore tells Luce to test both independently and preserve whichever actually works. citeturn504286search0\n\nOnce Luce returns this, bring the raw return here. I’ll reconcile it into a **Bedrock utilization map: model → job → cost → context → routing priority**, so we can stretch the AWS runway instead of burning it blindly. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790213668.049697, "end_turn": true, "id": "5d4ac911-6d7d-4db3-a856-43aa13a12a69", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-responses-api.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 476, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 7, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 1}, {"ref_index": 2, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 1}, {"ref_index": 4, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 1}, {"ref_index": 6, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 1}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "DeepSeek V3.2 - Amazon Bedrock", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-c