 in `OPENAI_BASE_URL`. AWS documents those separately. citeturn526976search0turn526976search1\n\n`AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` is valid for Boto3/Bedrock-style authentication use cases, so its presence is not wrong. It just does **not prove the Mantle/OpenAI-compatible path is configured**. citeturn526976search3turn526976search5\n\n## Step 2 — do only this\n\nWe are **not invoking a model yet**.\n\nWe are only going to prove that the existing 116-character credential can authenticate to the **Ohio Mantle model-list endpoint**.\n\nRun these three commands:\n\n```powershell\n$env:OPENAI_API_KEY = $env:AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK\n```\n\n```powershell\n$env:OPENAI_BASE_URL = \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\"\n```\n\nThen verify configuration **without exposing the key**:\n\n```powershell\nWrite-Host \"OPENAI_API_KEY=PRESENT length=$($env:OPENAI_API_KEY.Length)\"\nWrite-Host \"OPENAI_BASE_URL=$env:OPENAI_BASE_URL\"\n```\n\nYou should see:\n\n```text\nOPENAI_API_KEY=PRESENT length=116\nOPENAI_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1\n```\n\n### Stop there.\n\nDo **not** make the API request yet.\n\nPaste me exactly those two output lines.\n\nThen Step 3 will be a single **GET `/models`** request. That costs us no inference tokens and will tell us whether this credential + Ohio + Mantle combination authenticates at all. AWS explicitly documents `/models` as the Mantle model-discovery endpoint. citeturn526976search0\n\nThat is the cleanest possible next test."]}, "create_time": 1790215593.358442, "end_turn": true, "id": "e156b09d-1906-4807-b1bd-7631ed834506", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "kvm09a", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "sgzga0", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "zf2wzd", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "6yu3in", "preview_language": nul