ssfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yep — that error is **our formatting query**, not Bedrock. Fun one. 😄\n\n`inferenceTypesSupported` is a **list** (`ON_DEMAND`, `PROVISIONED`, or both), and AWS CLI’s `table` formatter is choking because one “cell” can contain multiple elements. AWS confirms that field is a list. citeturn859665search0turn859665search4\n\nSo we simplify.\n\nRun **this one command only**:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock list-foundation-models `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --by-provider Amazon `\n  --query \"modelSummaries[].{ModelId:modelId,Name:modelName,Status:modelLifecycle.status}\" `\n  --output table\n```\n\nThat avoids the nested list entirely and uses AWS’s native `--by-provider Amazon` filter. citeturn859665search0\n\n### What this test tells us\n\nIf it returns Amazon models, we have proven:\n\n```text\nus-east-2\n    ↓\nBedrock control-plane API\n    ↓\nAmazon foundation models visible\n```\n\nWe are **still not invoking anything**.\n\nIf the table works, paste it here and we’ll choose the exact Amazon/Nova candidate from **your account’s live inventory**, not from documentation.\n\nAnd document this failure as:\n\n```text\nFAILED TEST:\nAWS CLI --output table with inferenceTypesSupported nested list\n\nERROR:\nRow should have 1 elements, instead it has 2\n\nCLASSIFICATION:\nLOCAL OUTPUT-FORMATTING / JMESPATH ISSUE\n\nNOT:\nAuthentication\nRegion\nBedrock connectivity\nModel access\nBilling\n```\n\nSo nothing broke. We just asked the AWS CLI table renderer to eat an array for breakfast."]}, "create_time": 1790215930.819409, "end_turn": true, "id": "1dd5bd9d-730e-4e60-8c2a-d61d4ce08c03", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "hcwg06", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "20zmnk",