ata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["**Bam indeed.** That cleanly proves the second lane.\n\nYour `us-east-2` Bedrock **runtime inventory** sees these Amazon models as `ACTIVE`:\n\n```text\namazon.nova-pro-v1:0      Nova Pro\namazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0   Nova 2 Lite\namazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0\namazon.nova-lite-v1:0     Nova Lite\namazon.nova-micro-v1:0    Nova Micro\n```\n\nSo we now have two independently proven paths:\n\n**Mantle/OpenAI-compatible lane**\n```text\nus-east-2\n→ bedrock-mantle\n→ moonshotai.kimi-k2.5\n→ successful live inference\n```\n\n**Amazon-native runtime lane**\n```text\nus-east-2\n→ bedrock control/runtime inventory\n→ Nova models ACTIVE\n```\n\nThat explains a lot. **Kimi lives on the Mantle lane; Nova is showing up on the classic Bedrock runtime lane.** Same AWS account, same region, different invocation surface.\n\nThe next clean test is **Nova 2 Lite** because it is active and cheap enough for a tiny control probe. I would *not* use the Mantle URL for it. We should call it through `bedrock-runtime`.\n\nRun this next, and only this:\n\n```powershell\n$body = @{\n    messages = @(\n        @{\n            role = \"user\"\n            content = @(\n                @{\n                    text = \"Return exactly: NOVA_OK\"\n                }\n            )\n        }\n    )\n    inferenceConfig = @{\n        maxTokens = 20\n        temperature = 0\n    }\n} | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock-runtime converse `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --model-id amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0 `\n  --messages '[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Return exactly: NOVA_OK\"}]}]' `\n  --inference-config '{\"maxTokens\":20,\"temperature\":0}'\n```\n\nIf that succeeds, we will have proven:\n\n```text\nAmazon credits ✅\nKimi on Mantle ✅\nNova on Runtime ✅\nOhio region ✅\nIAM identity ✅\nBoth API surfaces ✅\n```\n\nAt that point the issue is not “Bedrock is broken.” It is **routing the right model to the right endpoint/API**.\n\nAnd that is exactly the kind of thing worth documenting as a permanent Bedrock recovery/runbook so we never burn another hour rediscovering it. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1790215964.696621, "end_turn": true, "id": "1ed4a5a2-cd76-40c5-b9a7-bd594bb7a024", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "np41r1", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "7arh8a", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "mrqbho", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "zhewv0", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "vora6w", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "5": {"edited": false, "id": "ajlaoo", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 2022, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 2013, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "87dae6f5-5074-4c1e-9423-c287569b2426", "request_id": "c47cbbe7-ea63-4367-8e51-717bab8c0874", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "46b218f9-b4a3-49d4-9407-a5cfd5988a4a", "working_turn_id": "46b218f9-b4a3-49d4-9407-a5cfd5988a4a"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790216056.71038, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "conten