use the `us.` CRIS-prefixed model ID. citeturn758088search7turn758088search2\n\nSo your inventory command was correct: it showed the underlying model exists and is `ACTIVE`.\n\nBut for actual inference, **the callable ID is different**.\n\n## Do one clean Nova 2 test\n\nRun:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock-runtime converse `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --model-id us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0 `\n  --messages file://\"$env:TEMP\\nova-messages.json\" `\n  --inference-config file://\"$env:TEMP\\nova-inference.json\"\n```\n\nBut since we haven't created those two files yet, let's avoid another quoting circus.\n\nRun these first:\n\n```powershell\n@'\n[\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Return exactly: NOVA_OK\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n'@ | Set-Content \"$env:TEMP\\nova-messages.json\" -Encoding ascii\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```powershell\n@'\n{\n  \"maxTokens\": 20,\n  \"temperature\": 0\n}\n'@ | Set-Content \"$env:TEMP\\nova-inference.json\" -Encoding ascii\n```\n\nThen the actual invocation:\n\n```powershell\naws bedrock-runtime converse `\n  --region us-east-2 `\n  --model-id us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0 `\n  --messages file://\"$env:TEMP\\nova-messages.json\" `\n  --inference-config file://\"$env:TEMP\\nova-inference.json\"\n```\n\nAWS currently lists Nova 2 Lite as supporting **Converse**, so this is a valid operation; the likely defect in our prior call was the raw model ID rather than the required US inference-profile ID. citeturn758088search0turn758088search3\n\n### Document the finding like this\n\n```text\nTEST:\nbedrock-runtime Converse\nRegion: us-east-2\nModel ID: amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n\nRESULT:\nValidationException — Operation not allowed\n\nCLASSIFICATION:\nINFERENCE ROUTING / MODEL ID\n\nROOT CAUSE CANDIDATE:\nNova 2 Lite in US regions requires US CRIS inference profile:\nus.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n\nNOT INDICATED:\nCredential failure\nNetwork failure\nBilling failure\nRegion connectivity failure\nJSON parsing failure\n```\n\nAnd this is exactly why the earlier Playground behavior was confusing: **“model exists in region” and “raw model ID is directly invokable” are not the same thing anymore.**\n\nRun that `us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0` test. If it returns `NOVA_OK`, we've cracked the Amazon-native problem too."]}, "create_time": 1790216172.729494, "end_turn": true, "id": "1775cff2-8a0e-4081-bf25-a35a9141bcd9", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "veyxef", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "b7sbtm", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "nqjux6", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "olfshu", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "e01o05", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "5": {"edited": false, "id": "4m87rn", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "6": {"edited": false, "id": "p2gsja", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/getting-started-console.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 633, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 7, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 2, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Using the Invoke API - Amazon Nova", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/using-invoke-api.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}], "title": "Getting started with Amazon Nova in the Amazon Bedrock console - Amazon Nova", "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/nova2-userguide/getting-started