w the leading explanation for the Nova 2 Lite failure**, but with one precise twist:\n\nAWS currently shows **Nova 2 Lite is *not* available for single-region inference in `us-east-2`**. Ohio supports it through **US Geo** or **Global cross-region inference** instead. citeturn470143search1turn470143search0\n\nThat reconciles the apparently contradictory facts we just observed:\n\n- `amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0` appears as **ACTIVE** in the Bedrock model catalog.\n- Direct `Converse` against the raw ID in `us-east-2` returns **`ValidationException: Operation not allowed`**.\n- AWS says the US cross-region ID from Ohio is:\n\n```text\nus.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\nand Ohio is a supported **source region** for that US Geo inference profile. citeturn470143search0\n\nThere are actually **two separate failures** in your last test sequence:\n\n```text\nNo such file or directory: nova-messages.json\n```\n\nThat one is purely local — the temp file didn't exist.\n\nThen:\n\n```text\nValidationException: Operation not allowed\n```\n\nThat one is AWS/runtime routing.\n\n## Let's remove every other variable\n\nDon't use the temp files. Don't use raw `amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0`.\n\nRun **one** command with the US inference profile, but use PowerShell's stop-parsing operator so it doesn't destroy the JSON:\n\n```powershell\naws --% bedrock-runtime converse --region us-east-2 --model-id us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0 --messages \"[{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Return exactly: NOVA_OK\\\"}]}]\" --inference-config \"{\\\"maxTokens\\\":20,\\\"temperature\\\":0}\"\n```\n\nIf that still gives us grief over Windows quoting, I want to switch to a tiny PowerShell-generated JSON file in the **current directory**, not `%TEMP%`, so we can visibly confirm it exists before invoking.\n\n### One more useful discovery\n\nThe older **Nova Lite** is different. AWS shows `amazon.nova-lite-v1:0` has **direct in-region support in Ohio**, whereas Nova **2** Lite does not. citeturn470143search2\n\nSo we now have an excellent A/B control:\n\n```text\nNova Lite:\namazon.nova-lite-v1:0\nOhio direct inference supported\n\nNova 2 Lite:\namazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\nOhio direct inference NOT supported\nUS Geo ID required:\nus.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0\n```\n\nIf needed, we can test old Nova Lite directly and Nova 2 Lite via the `us.` profile. That will prove the routing distinction beyond doubt.\n\nAnd yes — **I saved the full Mantle inventory you just extracted**, including Kimi 2.5, Kimi Thinking, GLM 5, DeepSeek V3.2, Grok 4.3, the OpenAI 5.x models, Qwen, Mistral, Nemotron, MiniMax, Gemma, and Claude Haiku 4.5, along with the fact that Kimi 2.5 has already passed live inference. memcite\n\nAfter we crack Nova, I absolutely want to do the **super-extraction by price**. That model list is much richer than I expected, and with $159.26 sitting there we can build a very serious GCE routing map."]}, "create_time": 1790216310.009438, "end_turn": true, "id": "a7c4537f-5c2b-4bc4-a157-1ee1008dc478", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "1gci4d", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "8691eo", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "6glxwh", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "3": {"edited": false, "id": "5x85c9", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "4": {"edited": false, "id": "ce719u", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "([AWS Documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/models-region-compatibility.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 337, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "AWS Documentation", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 1, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "t