nded", "request_id": "2354e6bf-dcc1-46ab-9348-bf842c7971f4", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "9ad39b40-fccf-4b16-8097-db50852cd880", "working_turn_id": "9ad39b40-fccf-4b16-8097-db50852cd880"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {"real_author": "tool:web"}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["That changes the diagnosis **materially**.\n\n`PeteW` inherits **AdministratorAccess** through the `GCE` group. So absent a permissions boundary, SCP, or some service-side account restriction, ordinary IAM permissions are **not** the problem.\n\nAnd I found something very relevant: AWS re:Post has current reports of this **exact** pattern — `ValidationException: Operation not allowed` on Bedrock `Converse`, even when IAM is correct, the model is active, billing is valid, and the inference profile exists. In those cases the issue was an **account/service-level Bedrock runtime restriction/allowlisting condition**, not malformed JSON or missing `bedrock:InvokeModel`. citeturn362763search0turn362763search2\n\nSo our state is now:\n\n```text\nPeteW IAM user                     ✅\nGCE group membership               ✅\nAdministratorAccess via GCE        ✅\nBedrock control-plane access       ✅\nNova 2 Lite profile ACTIVE         ✅\nUS CRIS profile resolves           ✅\nMantle inference (Kimi 2.5)        ✅\nClassic Runtime Converse           ❌ \"Operation not allowed\"\n```\n\nThat is a **very distinctive split**.\n\n## One more IAM sanity check\n\nBefore I call this account/runtime-side, I want to rule out a permissions boundary on `PeteW`.\n\nRun only:\n\n```powershell\naws iam get-user `\n  --user-name PeteW `\n  --query \"User.PermissionsBoundary\" `\n  --output json\n```\n\nIf it returns:\n\n```text\nnull\n```\n\nthen there is no user permissions boundary constraining that AdministratorAccess.\n\nAfter that, the remaining high-value checks are **not more credential rotations** and **not more IAM policy changes**. We would inspect:\n\n1. whether the AWS account belongs to an Organization/SCP,\n2. Bedrock Runtime quotas/allowlisting state,\n3. direct Nova Lite vs Nova 2 Lite behavior,\n4. and, if necessary, the AWS Support/account-activation path.\n\nAWS re:Post specifically documents cases where token-generating Bedrock Runtime operations sit at account quotas of `0` and return this exact `Operation not allowed` error even though listing models/profiles works. citeturn362763search2\n\nSo you did, in fact, set IAM up pretty well. **AdministratorAccess through the GCE group is a coherent design.** The evidence is moving away from “Don misconfigured permissions” and toward **“Bedrock Runtime is gated on the account while Mantle is not.”**"]}, "create_time": 1790216581.539022, "end_turn": true, "id": "4fe7e72c-9582-421f-afd9-f26e1eddc946", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "xb0uq6", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "k2fxzp", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "2": {"edited": false, "id": "jjpu6z", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}}, "content_references": [{"alt": "([Repost](https://www.repost.aws/questions/QUQa_rMpLJSUC6luOZjwxEpQ/validation-exception-operation-not-allowed-on-bedrock-converse-api-nova-iam-correct-billing-active-key-rotated?utm_source=chatgpt.com))", "end_idx": 711, "error": null, "fallback_items": null, "items": [{"attribution": "Repost", "attribution_segments": null, "attributions": null, "hue": null, "pub_date": null, "refs": [{"ref_index": 0, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}, {"ref_index": 2, "ref_type": "search", "turn_index": 0}], "snippet": "", "supporting_websites": [{"attribution": "Repost", "pub_date": null, "snippet": "", "title": "Bedrock on-demand inference quotas all 0 wit