va quota remediation\n```\n\nDo not solve it.\n\nAlso list any unverified visible Mantle models that should not yet be relied upon.\n\n---\n\n## J. ROLLBACK\n\nGive the exact rollback procedure.\n\n---\n\n## K. CONTINUITY ANSWER\n\nAnswer:\n\n> If Don's direct Kimi / GLM / OpenAI provider access disappeared right now, can GCE continue terminal-based local-file work through Amazon Bedrock Mantle using the new bridge?\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nYES / PARTIAL / NO\n```\n\nwith evidence.\n\n---\n\n## L. CONFIDENCE\n\nGive a concise percentage based on live evidence.\n\n---\n\n# 22. SUCCESS DEFINITION\n\nThis mission is complete when all of the following are true:\n\n```text\n[ ] Existing AWS bearer secret reused safely\n[ ] Bedrock Mantle provider added locally\n[ ] us-east-2 Mantle endpoint used\n[ ] Kimi K2.5 invoked through the local terminal consumer\n[ ] Terminal/local orchestrator reads a real local GCE file\n[ ] Kimi reasons over that file successfully\n[ ] No source file modified during acceptance test\n[ ] Existing direct providers remain intact\n[ ] At least one additional verified model alias exposed or tested\n[ ] Rollback documented\n[ ] Nova/classic-runtime issue remains isolated and deferred\n```\n\n---\n\n# 23. IMPLEMENTATION DOCTRINE\n\nDo not make this larger than it is.\n\nAWS inference already works.\n\nThe missing piece is local consumption.\n\n**Use the existing orchestrator to provide tools and files.  \nUse Bedrock Mantle only as the inference backend.  \nAdd the smallest reversible bridge.  \nProve it.  \nStop.**\n\n---\n\n# SESSION FOOTER EXPECTATION\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nSTATUS:\nCONFIDENCE:\nOUTCOME:\nFILES MODIFIED:\nPROVIDER ADDED:\nMODELS VERIFIED THROUGH TERMINAL:\nLOCAL FILE TEST:\nOPEN ITEMS:\nDEFERRED:\nROLLBACK:\nDON INPUT NEEDED:\nNEXT ROUTE:\n```\n:::\n\nOne thing I intentionally made explicit in Nico's mission: Luce found that the local stack currently has **no active consumer pointing at Mantle**, despite the API itself being healthy; that's the implementation gap Nico is solving. fileciteturn0file0L69-L87\n\nAnd the acceptance test is based on your actual objective, not an AWS smoke test: **Bedrock model + terminal agent + real local GCE file + no modification**. Luce's own continuity finding was that this single config bridge is what turns Bedrock from latent capability into an operational fallback. fileciteturn0file0L114-L127"]}, "create_time": 1790217060.793377, "end_turn": true, "id": "942d0091-e5b1-4366-9c68-884a55c33cc7", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 19178, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "9233084a-7ac9-4763-85e5-e36b1a2ccdef", "cited_message_idx": 214, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_946b6a34ceec8191af28738f6dbbb636", "line_range": [69, 87], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 0, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_0000000067088230a6b8119a3fcae9cf", "name": "Pasted text.txt", "source": "my_files", "text": "F. LOCAL CONFIGURATION FINDINGS\nVerified facts (exact locations):\n1. ~/.secrets/master-secrets.env — only key: AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK (value never printed; masked sha12=6F73EC728826). No expiry annotation found in-file.", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 19149}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 19509, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "9233084a-7ac9-4763-85e5-e36b1a2ccdef", "cited_message_idx": 214, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_946b6a34ceec8191af2